<div class="brain-explainer">
  <section id="brain-context" aria-labelledby="brain-context-title">
    <h2 class="sr-only" id="brain-context-title">Why I built Second Brain</h2>
    <figure class="answer-preview">
      <div class="example-question">
        <span class="question-label">Example question</span>
        <p>“What project did we make last May that used liquid-metal graphics?”</p>
      </div>
      <div class="answer-path">
        <div class="rag-node">
          <h3>Second Brain</h3>
          <p>Finds related project evidence by meaning, exact terms, and date.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="answer-connector"><span>retrieves evidence</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></div>
        <div class="answer-card">
          <h3>Source-backed answer</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Project and date</li>
            <li>Liquid-metal visual references</li>
            <li>Links to the original files</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>A team member can ask in natural language and receive the project context with links to the evidence behind it.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="context-note">Studio knowledge is spread across files, conversations, media, and people. Founders and directors repeatedly stop to find links and answer routine questions. Second Brain lets every team member ask directly, without interrupting someone else or holding back because a question feels too small.</p>
    <p class="status-note"><span class="pause-mark" aria-hidden="true">Ⅱ</span><span><strong>Development in progress.</strong> Currently paused due to budget constraints.</span></p>
  </section>

  <nav class="brain-nav" aria-label="Second Brain sections">
    <a href="#brain-context">Why I built it</a>
    <a href="#brain-tour">Product tour</a>
