  <section id="brain-agents" aria-labelledby="brain-agents-title">
    <div class="section-copy">
      <h2 id="brain-agents-title">Give the agent evidence it can cite.</h2>
      <p>A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server lets an AI agent query the archive and read the wiki. The retrieval tool returns evidence; the calling agent composes the final answer.</p>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <div class="agent-exchange">
        <div class="exchange-row"><strong>AI agent</strong><div><span class="exchange-verb">asks for relevant evidence</span><code>brain_query(question)</code></div><strong>Second Brain</strong></div>
        <div class="exchange-row response"><strong>AI agent</strong><div><span class="exchange-verb">returns fragments and confidence</span><span>Text + source IDs + file context</span></div><strong>Second Brain</strong></div>
        <div class="answer-contract"><h3>The answer contract</h3><div><p><strong>Cite the claim.</strong><span>Attach the relevant source ID to important facts.</span></p><p><strong>Expose uncertainty.</strong><span>State the returned confidence. Keep conflicting facts visible.</span></p><p><strong>Leave gaps visible.</strong><span>Say when the evidence is insufficient.</span></p></div></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>These are the instructions for an agent using the memory. Retrieval supplies the evidence; following the citation contract remains the agent’s responsibility.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="brain-status" aria-labelledby="brain-status-title">
    <div class="section-copy">
      <h2 id="brain-status-title">I designed the product, retrieval, and interface.</h2>
      <p>I defined the product, designed the retrieval and evidence model, built the FastAPI backend and React interface, and used AI agents throughout development. Budget constraints paused the project before completion.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="state-grid">
      <div><h3>Implemented locally</h3><ul><li>Hybrid retrieval and source-linked results</li><li>Wiki with separate AI and human blocks</li><li>Graph, people records, and review tools</li><li>React interface, FastAPI backend, and MCP server</li></ul></div>
      <div class="unfinished"><h3>Still needs work</h3><ul><li>Extraction quality across complex source formats</li><li>Summary accuracy and stronger evidence context</li><li>Retrieval calibration and operational hardening</li><li>Dedicated safe data for a public product demo</li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <p class="integration-note">Connecting Second Brain to the SHUM Telegram Assistant remains a future direction. There is no completed production integration.</p>
    <details class="implementation-notes">
      <summary>Implementation behind the diagrams</summary>
      <div>
        <p>The diagrams describe mechanisms in the Second Brain source, rather than a live product session.</p>
        <dl><div><dt>Ingest</dt><dd><code>pipeline/ingest_*.py</code> extracts text, image descriptions, transcripts, video summaries, and source metadata.</dd></div><div><dt>Retrieval</dt><dd><code>pipeline/retrieval.py</code> combines semantic, keyword, and temporal candidates.</dd></div><div><dt>Wiki</dt><dd><code>pipeline/wiki_blocks.py</code> preserves human blocks and writes AI-block history.</dd></div><div><dt>Agent access</dt><dd><code>mcp_server/server.py</code> exposes source retrieval and wiki tools.</dd></div><div><dt>Interface</dt><dd>React, Vite, and TypeScript over a FastAPI API; ChromaDB and SQLite FTS5 store the search indexes.</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</div>

